{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/344515-glamour-gathering","id":344515,"title":"Glamour Gathering","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-19T02:51:45-08:00","id":344515,"title":"Glamour Gathering","content":"At the moment I am running my first Changeling chronicle and I am having some questions about glamour gathering about which I would like some second opinion/suggestions. The rules of glamour gathering are fairly simple and streight forward. The player select an emotion and a method, the storyteller assigns skills and a modifier, and the check is made with each success generating 1 glamour. From what I gather though the rules don't discuss those modifiers, only mentioning that quick rushes of emotions incur penalties (in other words: generate less glamour). It never even mentions how much time gathering glamour costs, although the mechanic again suggests it can be a matter of moments.<br /> <br /> Game mechanically this is no issue. It just means that in general glamour is easy to get. Since at the current powerlevel contracts are not particular powerful unlimittedless glamour does not really impact my game from a power perspective. It does clash with what is implied about glamour in other sections though. Why bother with the hunting ground merrit if you can gather glamour simply by acting like the crazy homeless guy on the streets (although that will eventually get you in trouble with the cops)? Why mention glamour tithes and rewards between lieges and followers? There are better things to gain compared to a measily 2 glamour per month. How does this work with the generic suggestion that glamour is somewhat rare and hard to get?<br /> <br /> Now, in my current game at least most of the players ignore the mechanics to some point. They make work to get a more permanent source of glamour through the story by finding the right kind of job such as for example working at a hospital (which is not easy for a newly returned Changeling). Still, others ignore story in this particular case and just use the mechanics, not because they are bad roleplayers, just because this aspect of the game is not their cup of tea. So any suggestions on how to penalize glamour hunting checks through modifiers that make that quick rush much harder, but not impossible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T09:05:16-08:00","id":344828,"title":"","content":"One suggestion that comes to mind is to ask the players, when harvesting glamour, whether they're actively causing the emotion or passively absorbing a feeling that's already there (I recall one of the books mentioning a changeling watching a city riot from a rooftop and soaking up the anger). Passively absorbing sorrow at a funeral or desire on a dancefloor might penalize their harvest roll. On the other hand, actively causing a rush of emotion might actually give them a bonus to the roll, depending on the circumstances; however, this comes with its own complications. You do your hardest to make a man at a bar lust after you, and now he won't leave you alone. You spook some normies coming home from a night out and the next day you're accosted by the police. Extra consequences I'd wager should most likely happen on either a dramatic failure (since that's the sort of thing a dramatic failure functions for) or an exceptional success (representing the overpowering strength of the emotion). It gives the players a choice to make every time they need a fix.<br /> <br /> The trickle of glamour from pledges is kind of weird, though I imagine that changelings dedicated to that approach just make a lot of pledges with the glamour boon. I also imagine that they're the sorts who either can't, won't, or feel like they can't interact with humanity on an emotionally-connecting level.<br /> <br /> <i>Blood &amp; Smoke</i> has a section on running feeding scenes that could be adapted for Changeling with a little finagling, if that's your thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T11:13:29-08:00","id":344973,"title":"","content":"Side question - <b>should not Emotion Harvesting burn a targeted mortals Willpower points equal to gained Glamour?</b> Mortal is under powerful emotions ( often meant in general system as spending Willpower to get there ) and after this it's &quot;taken&quot; by changelings, leaving him a bit &quot;dried&quot;? Also, Willpower points works as Health boxes in &quot;not serious mental combats&quot;, like oneiromancy or Astral Realms &quot;wounds&quot; system. I think that changelings are a bit &quot;hurting&quot; mortals when they Harvest, making Lost a bit &quot;psychic vampires&quot; more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T11:49:41-08:00","id":344987,"title":"","content":"You know, I thought there was something about that in <i>Rites of Spring</i>, but I just checked, and the only harvest-related optional rules in that book are all about upping the feel of glamour as a sort of powerful drug. However, I'm pretty sure there's something on the subject in <i>Dream Catchers</i>. Something about putting little dots over the victim's Wits score, leading the lethargy and ennui.<br /> <br /> Actually, now that I'm rereading <i>Rites of Spring</i>, harvesting glamour sounds less like absorbing a human being's emotions and more like just teasing them to the surface and riding the wave. Or something. The metaphysics of glamour are never fully explained, and seem to vary from book to book. <i>Rites of Spring</i> makes glamour sound like a hallucinogen, while the opening fiction to <i>Swords at Dawn</i> almost seems to imply that the point of glamour is to generate snippets of narrative for the Wyrd. So. Hmm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T20:46:25-08:00","id":345374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/344515-glamour-gathering?p=344987#post344987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I thought there was something about that in <i>Rites of Spring</i>, but I just checked, and the only harvest-related optional rules in that book are all about upping the feel of glamour as a sort of powerful drug. However, I'm pretty sure there's something on the subject in <i>Dream Catchers</i>. Something about putting little dots over the victim's Wits score, leading the lethargy and ennui.<br /> <br /> Actually, now that I'm rereading <i>Rites of Spring</i>, harvesting glamour sounds less like absorbing a human being's emotions and more like just teasing them to the surface and riding the wave. Or something. The metaphysics of glamour are never fully explained, and seem to vary from book to book. <i>Rites of Spring</i> makes glamour sound like a hallucinogen, while the opening fiction to <i>Swords at Dawn</i> almost seems to imply that the point of glamour is to generate snippets of narrative for the Wyrd. So. Hmm.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'm not up to Rites in my reread just yet, I distinctly remember - hang on\u2026 yep, corebook:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>&quot;Harvesting Glamour,&quot; p89</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Harvesting Glamour in this fashion doesn\u2019t actually drain energy; the mortal does not suddenly feel less emotional as the changeling harvests the mortal\u2019s feelings. Many changelings take comfort in this fact, interpreting the lack of visible harm as less of a violation. However, whispers tell of mortals who are subjected to regular harvesting over a long period of time eventually losing some indescribable, yet vital spark. While these ravaged souls remain the stuff of rumors, it is enough of a fear that many changelings avoid tapping the same resource too often, especially in the case of friends or loved ones. Just in case.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's nearer to generating Essence than, say, running a feeding scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T20:49:02-08:00","id":345394,"title":"","content":"Oh, weird. Fair enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T21:33:47-08:00","id":345406,"title":"","content":"Honestly, feeding on a single person for a long period of time probably causes even more long-term damage than vampire-induced anemia does...without any supernatural cause.<br /> <br /> Just think of the kind of psychological damage you would suffer if you were forced to feel anger, fear, or sorrow all the time. Hence why a moral changeling is an eat-and-run person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T21:47:37-08:00","id":345417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/344515-glamour-gathering?p=345406#post345406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, feeding on a single person for a long period of time probably causes even more long-term damage than vampire-induced anemia does...without any supernatural cause.<br /> <br /> Just think of the kind of psychological damage you would suffer if you were forced to feel anger, fear, or sorrow all the time. Hence why a moral changeling is an eat-and-run person.</div> </div> </div> </div>To point to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/246393-fairy-tales-and-ghost-stories-shared-likenesses-of-fae-and-the-dead\">a topic of personal interest</a> as a comparison, having a ghost Fettered to you is not fun for roughly identical reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T21:52:49-08:00","id":345430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/344515-glamour-gathering?p=344987#post344987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <i>Rites of Spring</i> makes glamour sound like a hallucinogen, while the opening fiction to <i>Swords at Dawn</i> almost seems to imply that the point of glamour is to generate snippets of narrative for the Wyrd. So. Hmm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those two points are more related than you imagine.<br /> <br /> Glamour is essentially Essence of Emotional Catharsis, with some caveats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T03:33:03-08:00","id":345620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/344515-glamour-gathering?p=345374#post345374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's nearer to generating Essence than, say, running a feeding scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not liking it a bit, as all major templates of WoD <b>are</b> monsters, one way or another, most time predators ( vampires, werewolves, demons, mummies maybe? ). With changeling only &quot;generating things&quot; in humans, it's not have enough &quot;claw&quot; as temporary draining a bit of psychic energy from mortals. It makes changelings &quot;almost non-monsters&quot;, more fantasy characters than horror ones, in the WoD setting that is said all the time &quot;we make a horror game here&quot;.<br /> <br /> I will probably left a Glamour Harvesting having effect on Willpower of mortal as house rule, but I'm thanked for clearing official stand from book for now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T06:53:48-08:00","id":345736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It makes changelings &quot;almost non-monsters&quot;, more fantasy characters than horror ones, in the WoD setting that is said all the time &quot;we make a horror game here&quot;. </div> </div> </div>YMMV, but there is plenty of horror in Changeling outside Glamor Harvesting, namely in themes of what Changelings went through and how they cope with them. It's a thing of personal horror towards which WoD generally leans. What your PC personally experiences is as important as his/her impact on other.<br /> <br /> To be a figure taking part in horror you don't have to be necessarily a monster (though there are some more fucked up Changelings out there, but conversely mortals can be as monstrous or even more than non-mortals), you may be a victim or play both roles.<br /> <br /> &quot;If, for argument's sake, you were to write a story with me in the lead role, it would be certainly a tragedy&quot;. That quote is probably what may describe some WoD PCs out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 12-20-2014, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T09:43:55-08:00","id":345811,"title":"","content":"Got to agree with Kat here; you don't need to be the monster to be in a horror story. Most often, quite the opposite. Changelings deal with a half-dozen kinds of horror before breakfast; their minds and bodies have been changed by alien experiences, yet no-one but a select few can see it. Reality itself might be a lie, and danger lurks around every corner. Every door, every window, every mirror is a possible portal through which the Gentry or one of their lapdogs or an army of goblins might come storming. Everyone you love is a potential weapon against you, but, if you don't keep them close, it becomes oh so difficult to remember just what reality is and isn't; so much harder to believe <i>this</i> is true.<br /> <br /> Changelings are victims as much as villains.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, you have the ability to make Pledges, which grant a fair deal more power when dealing with mortals, and feed off of mortal emotions. Even if you don't induce the emotion yourself, you're encouraged to maintain it and, while this can be benign, not all Changelings will take that path. Miami explicitly has Winter Court members who basically use the drug trade to feed their habit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T10:55:49-08:00","id":345903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Reality itself might be a lie, and danger lurks around every corner. Every door, every window, every mirror is a possible portal through which the Gentry or one of their lapdogs or an army of goblins might come storming. Everyone you love is a potential weapon against you, but, if you don't keep them close, it becomes oh so difficult to remember just what reality is and isn't; so much harder to believe this is true. </div> </div> </div>Also such situation may happen that the Keeper in fact does not care about his former possessions and does not do anything to return them back in the fold but 'his' Changeling(s) are so paranoid that their are on constant alert anyway.<br /> <br /> Options are limitless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T11:42:20-08:00","id":345969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/344515-glamour-gathering?p=345620#post345620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not liking it a bit,</div> </div> </div> </div>Color me shocked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It makes changelings &quot;almost non-monsters&quot;, more fantasy characters than horror ones, in the WoD setting that is said all the time &quot;we make a horror game here&quot;. </div> </div> </div>If you don't understand the horror in a complete stranger going out of their way to elicit a strong (and, due to comparative ease of generation, probably negative) emotional reaction in you with no warning or intent to resolve that sudden derailing of your day, you're not thinking about the implications of this beyond &quot;but it doesn't immediately drain a single individual!&quot; and I have no obligation to sit through the process of convincing you that dragging strangers into soap-opera-level shocking twists is a problem.<br /> <br /> I answered calamar's question to answer calamar's question, not to get dragged into this personal-opinion horsepucky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T06:18:38-08:00","id":347347,"title":"","content":"Personally I agree with Satchel, long term emotional manipulations are bad for the person, especially since the more common emotions the Changelings use are in general considered to be negative. Adding game mechanics do not change it. Of course, letting it drain something as Willpower makes glamour hunting an actual combat power, and a fairly effective one at that especially if you use the monster power rules from Hunter (which I do because I dislike memorizing and selecting the various contracts for opponents who at most will use three powers anyway). If you consider long term glamour collection from the same person risky to that person\u2019s mental health, using oaths to get glamour from a mortal is not such a bad idea. Unlike through regular gathering, you do not manipulate the person\u2019s emotions (usually anyway).<br /> <br /> Anyway, to summarize, incur penalties for gather glamour from:<br /> - quick burst of emotion<br /> - emotions generated through the actions of others (good suggestion)<br /> <br /> Now I just need to think about reasonable and somewhat consistent numbers\u2026<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T15:21:26-08:00","id":347754,"title":"","content":"If you want numbers, my recommendation is to consider what you'd call the &quot;standard&quot; feeding level - the level at which you'd get no bonuses or penalties - and then move about that. For example, if there's a requirement of intimacy in feeding, you might set the standard for feeding on Sorrow as a Changeling comforting a grieving person; Fear might require someone to experience a genuine tinge of dread, but no more so than, say, watching a horror movie.<br /> <br /> You can then, say, subtract -1 if the Changeling isn't the one responsible for the fear, but add +1 if they're feeding off of a crowd, providing an incentive for Changelings to stalk resonant places (hanging out in funeral homes, nightclubs, etc.).<br /> <br /> Bonuses:<br /> <br /> Changeling interacts intimately with the subject(s) ... +1<br /> Changeling induces the emotion in question personally ... +1<br /> Emotion is supernaturally enhanced .... +1<br /> Changeling is targeting a crowd .... +1<br /> Changeling is making themselves the focus of the emotion ... +1<br /> Changeling unveils their fae mien or some other blatantly obvious supernatural element .... +2<br /> Subject is in the grips of extreme emotions ... +2<br /> Experience takes place in an environment the Changeling has specially prepared for this .... +2<br /> Subject is at their utmost limits of emotional experience (heart-attack-inducing terror, suicidal depression, blinding rage, etc.) .... +3 to +5<br /> <br /> These bonuses naturally stack, meaning that a Changeling of the Autumn Court who, on Halloween, unveils their mien and chases a group of terrified children into an abandoned factory filled with hand-carved wooden grotesques and scares one of them to near-death reaps a very large harvest indeed.<br /> <br /> Penalties:<br /> <br /> Changeling doesn't interact personally with the target(s) ... -1<br /> Changeling forces an emotion using magic where there wasn't one before .... -1<br /> Crowd around the target is experiencing highly dissonant emotions (i,e, grieving widow at an amusement park) ... -1<br /> Environment is strongly dissonant with emotions being fed upon (i.e. trying to feed on sexual desire in a hospital morgue [necrophiles exempted]) .... -1<br /> Target only marginally feels the emotion in question (i.e. &quot;I kind of want a donut&quot; for desire) ... -2<br /> Target is in the grips of an extreme emotion other than the one trying to be fed upon (i.e. blinding rage when trying to feed upon sorrow) ... -3 to -5<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T15:48:20-08:00","id":347795,"title":"","content":"I have no issue with Glamour harvesting not, in and of itself, hurting people. Certainly, emotional manipulation can be harmful, and that is a good pitfall to have, but while I don't mind a game having the fuel stat be harmful to harvest, I don't think it always needs to be that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T02:03:35-08:00","id":348134,"title":"","content":"Considering Changelings cannot harvest from fellow Changelings, I am a bit hesitent to add bonuses for emotions directly enhanced by contracts or any magic for that matter.<br /> <br /> As for revealing the blatant supernatural element, except potentially indirectly (desire and fear are likely to be enhanced for some seemings/kiths), how would that make gathering glamour easier? Mind you, considering the price to be paid both to achieve such an effect and the consequences for ones Clarity, I doubt Changeling would often reveal their mien (loos all glamour to potentially gather a few more seems like a bad trade).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T05:45:39-08:00","id":348208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (loos all glamour to potentially gather a few more seems like a bad trade). </div> </div> </div>'<br /> If you are running on fumes anyway, it might be not so outlandish option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T13:13:11-08:00","id":348505,"title":"","content":"The reason the harvest is enhanced for emotions improved by magic - but penalized for emotions created by it - is for the sake of encouraging Changelings to &quot;salt the meat&quot;; to drive mortals to excess. It's exceptionally fae as far as conduct goes, and easily provides hooks for you as they make situations... Complicated. That guy you used a Contract on so you could feed off his Desire for the pretty young thing across the room? Turns out you did it a bit <i>too</i> well...<br /> <br /> As for showing off your mien, I was going for the notion that a Changeling who has dropped the Mask, be it because they're in the Hedge or otherwise, is going to add to the strangeness of a scene. They spark the mortal's senses. You could also add something about the Mask not getting in the way but that's just post-hoc justification. The real reason is to give Changelings a reason to show off.<br /> <br /> I chose the bonuses and penalties there because they introduce (what I think are) interesting complications and incentives for Changelings to show off. I like Changeling with a sense of desire to revel in one's fae nature as a perpetual temptation. If you don't like it, though, feel free to discard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T20:05:29-08:00","id":369345,"title":"","content":"Wait. So...changelings aren't scary enough without having to suck out your soul to feed their magic? I mean, without even glancing at Contracts or Tokens, a changeling can:<br /> <br /> 1. Twist your words into iron clad promises. Hyperbolically say &quot;Just kill me now&quot; becomes a demand for your friend to commit murder, and failure to do so can be a death sentence for him.<br /> <br /> 2. Step into your dreams to spy on your secret fantasies or twist your mind into terrible nightmares.<br /> <br /> 3. Twist fate to place you in the center of a poetic disaster.<br /> <br /> 4. Have instant access to a world of mad nightmares and thorn covered paths that leads everywhere in the human world...including the openings in your house. If they are willing to devote the time to find the right gate, that could creep out of the Hedge into your bedroom. And what's worse, once that door is open its easier for OTHER THINGS to come into your room as well.<br /> <br /> 5. Hide behind an iron clad illusion so that you cannot know where or who they are. And the only reliable way to see through that illusion is to make a deal with one of these things and agree to do whatever it might want you to do for so however long you desire to see through the illusion.<br /> <br /> 6. Oh yeah. Did we mention that basically all of the things that can do this shit are more or less broken and paranoid things who at best have to fight to maintain a firm grip on sanity, who might completely lose it if life doesn't go exactly their way. Basically, you are dealing with a borderline psychotic who can decide to do any of the above to you just cause you looked at them funny. <br /> <br /> And these are the NICE ones, the ones that can remember being human and can hope to have a grip on sanity. The stuff that hides deeper in the Fae realms....well, Changelings are just scratching the surface of the horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}